{"reference":"Psalms 41","book":"Psalms","chapter":41,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"A Book Boundary","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The closing praise in verse 13 also marks the end of the first of the Psalter’s five books. The arrangement of the Psalms into these books includes similar doxological boundaries after Psalms 72, 89, and 106.","verse_refs":["Psalms 41:13"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_psalms_041_440b9a5231b6fc95775275bb"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}